Date: Mon, 22 Jun 2026 00:42:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(leakage): eliminate confirmed data leakage + align code
 with manuscript (Q1 audit)

CRITICAL FIXES (see 39_CODE_AUDIT_CRITICAL_FINDINGS.md for full audit):

1. notebooks/03_feature_engineering.py
   - REMOVED full-sample (2005-2025) climatology computation for
     GHI_anom/CLOUD_anom/PRECTOT_anom/T2M_anom. These leaked future
     information into every walk-forward fold, including training data.
   - Added separate df_report (full-sample) ONLY for descriptive VIF/
     correlation diagnostics -- never used for any model fit.
   - df_model export no longer requires anomaly columns; they are
     computed fresh per-fold downstream via utils.get_split_data().

2. utils.py -- REWRITTEN, now actually imported by every notebook
   - NEW: expanding_climatology() -- the per-fold expanding-window
     climatology that the manuscript's Section 3.5 describes but that
     did not exist anywhere in the codebase prior to this commit.
   - NEW: climatology_baseline_predict() -- leakage-free climatological
     point-forecast baseline.
   - FIXED: skill_score() -- now requires an explicit y_clim_pred
     argument; the old version used y_true.mean() (the TEST SET's own
     mean) as the baseline, which is impossible in real forecasting.
   - FIXED: get_split_data() -- recomputes anomaly + A_x_B interaction
     features per-fold from training data only, instead of returning
     pre-leaked full-sample columns.
   - NEW: verify_no_feature_leakage() -- a real leakage guard that
     checks FEATURE VALUES, not just row-level date ordering (the
     original guard's assertion passed trivially while leakage existed).

3. notebooks/04_validation_framework.py
   - REMOVED ~190 lines of inline function definitions that duplicated
     (and diverged from) utils.py, making utils.py finally the single
     source of truth it was always intended to be.
   - Leakage-guard verification now uses verify_no_feature_leakage(),
     confirmed to detect real per-fold-vs-full-sample divergence for
     every one of the 9 folds.

4. notebooks/09_residual_diagnostics.py
   - FIXED the Climatology_baseline row in the final aggregate
     comparison table: was computed from the FULL 2015-2023 test
     period combined (using up to 8 years of future data to predict
     the earliest test year) -- exactly the aggregate baseline error
     the manuscript's Methods Section 3.5 says was identified and
     corrected, but which was still present in this notebook's actual
     code. Now uses per-fold expanding-window climatology.
   - Verified numerical impact: corrected baseline RMSE differs from
     the old buggy version by ~14% in end-to-end functional testing.

5. notebooks/05/06/07 -- walk-forward SkillScore formulas
   - All three notebooks used a SkillScore baseline of either the test
     set's own mean (05) or the test set's own standard deviation
     (06, 07) -- neither matches the manuscript's described per-fold
     climatological baseline, and all three were mutually inconsistent
     with each other. Unified via utils.skill_score() +
     utils.get_split_data() across all three notebooks.

HIGH-PRIORITY ALIGNMENT FIXES:

6. notebooks/02_target_reconstruction.py
   - Added L_monsoon and L_ENSO stochastic loss components. The
     manuscript (Table 2, Figure 6 caption) describes 7 components;
     only 5 existed in code prior to this commit.

7. notebooks/08_shap_analysis.py
   - Added the cross-fold SHAP stability check (full-sample vs fold-1
     vs fold-9) that the manuscript cites (Figure 10B, Table S1) but
     that had no corresponding implementation anywhere in the repo.
     This check actively WARNS if the stability claim does not hold
     for a given run, rather than silently assuming it does.
   - Fixed df_analysis to recompute anomaly features using the SAME
     2005-2023 window the pickled XGBoost model was actually trained
     on (notebook 07 Part C), preventing a silent train/explain
     feature mismatch.

8. notebooks/07_xgboost_model.py
   - BOOTSTRAP_SAMPLES: 50 -> 200 (code comment's own TODO, never
     previously applied: use 200 for final paper).
   - Bootstrap PI now adds back training-residual noise to each
     bootstrap prediction. The original implementation captured only
     parameter/estimation uncertainty, structurally guaranteeing
     under-coverage (consistent with the severely miscalibrated
     PICP=0.361 the manuscript reports and excludes from main
     reporting). Functional test: PICP improved to 0.713 (90% nominal)
     after this fix.
   - Hyperparameter search (Part A) and full-sample SHAP model (Part C)
     now also use per-fold/window-scoped anomaly recomputation,
     extending the leakage fix to these auxiliary fitting steps.

